Logout/Alert RCA: app/(tabs)/profile.tsx:60-74 wraps the destructive logout work (deregisterPush + disableBiometric + logout + router.replace('/login')) inside the second button of Alert.alert('Sign out', 'Are you sure...', [{Cancel}, {Sign out, destructive, onPress: ...}]). react-native-web's Alert module is a no-op stub — calling Alert.alert with buttons does NOT render any modal, does NOT call window.confirm, and does NOT invoke any button's onPress. Result on web preview: tap 'Sign out' → console silent → URL stays at /profile → user is stuck signed in. Reproduction: log in as trades.demo@safebase.com.au / Demo@1234 → navigate to /profile → click element with [data-testid='profile-logout-button']; observe URL unchanged, no `dialog` event in Playwright, no console message. The same Alert.alert pattern is used for capture-success, incident-saved, risk-saved, settings-saved alerts — all of which are unreachable on web. Mitigation: install a one-shot Alert shim for web. Suggested patch (src/lib/alert.web.ts, picked up by metro's .web.ts resolution, or imported once in app/_layout.tsx):
```ts
import { Alert, Platform } from 'react-native';
if (Platform.OS === 'web') {
  (Alert as any).alert = (title: string, message?: string, buttons?: any[]) => {
    const txt = [title, message].filter(Boolean).join('\n\n');
    const destructive = buttons?.find((b) => b.style === 'destructive') ?? buttons?.find((b) => (b.text ?? '').toLowerCase() !== 'cancel');
    const cancel = buttons?.find((b) => (b.style === 'cancel') || (b.text ?? '').toLowerCase() === 'cancel');
    const ok = (buttons && buttons.length > 1) ? window.confirm(txt) : (window.alert(txt), true);
    if (ok) destructive?.onPress?.();
    else cancel?.onPress?.();
  };
}
```
